// Annex C.9: "Clause 7 only applies to Verilog-AMS HDL." A connect rules block
// is the Clause 7 construct that names which connect modules a mixed-signal
// elaborator may insert (A.1.2 `connectrules_declaration ::= connectrules
// connectrules_identifier ; { connectrules_item } endconnectrules`), so a
// Verilog-A compiler must refuse the CONSTRUCT, not merely the keywords.
//
// C.16 lists connect, connectrules and endconnectrules among the keywords "not
// used by Verilog-A"; 16_unused_ams_words_rejected.va covers those spellings as
// identifiers, which is a different rule — a compiler could reserve every word
// and still elaborate the block.
//
// The construct one level down, `connectmodule`, is 26: the parser does not
// recover past this declaration, so a single file naming both would prove only
// whichever came first.
//
//! lrm C.9
//! lrm C.16
//! reject E0201
//! reject connectrules
connectrules annex_c_connectrules_rejected;
    connect a2d;
endconnectrules
